  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Rain showers are expected Sunday into Monday, with \nbest chances across Central NY as a slow moving Nor'easter grazes \nthe area.\n\nAn unseasonably strong coastal low off the New Jersey coast will \ncomplete a cyclonic loop to the south of Long Island tonight through \nSunday, with the low nearing the Jersey shore by late Sunday and \nSunday night. The westward drift in the position of the vertically \nstacked low will advect Atlantic moisture westward across NY/PA, \nwith thickening and lowering clouds. The first chance of showers \nwill reach central NY early Sunday morning, then will progress \ngradually westward as an inverted trough axis north of the low \ncenter rotates westward. Showers may reach the Genesee Valley and \nwestern Finger Lakes by early to mid afternoon. Far western New York \nshould stay dry most of Sunday, although a few light showers should \narrive by late afternoon or evening.\n\nThe coastal low is then forecast to slowly meander northeast along \nthe New England coast Sunday night through Tuesday, weakening with \ntime. The greatest rain chances and greatest western extent of the \nrain shield will be Sunday night, with showers then gradually \ntapering off and ending from west to east late Sunday night\nthrough Monday as the low weakens and moves northeast.",
